  clock: 5  # 5d7d
  nonce: 5d7d  # 5d7d
  message: "Partial progress 2026-06-24 (PR #4289, origin/dev=f0d3663c83): the NODE-BEARING half of the file-universe split is fixed (WI-dagif done) -- every path with content nodes now gets a kind=file anchor via the orchestrator chokepoint, so the contains tree is rootful for java/csharp/rust/generated files. REMAINING for WI-rajod (the full unification): centrality_scores keys are NON-source/nodeless paths (yaml/md/config) that still have no nodes, so the centrality_scores-subset-of-node-paths invariant is STILL violated. That is the F1+F4 co-release per D15: anchor the nodeless cohort (full file-anchor:F1) AND split the centrality surface (file-anchor:F4) in the SAME release -- else anchoring the nodeless cohort empties the Additional-Files surface (cli.py:8259-8261). Gated on the open human decision (correctness-strategy 6.6: file-anchor:F4 redefinition of the WI-rajod invariant must be stated, not implied). WI-rajod stays open for that co-release."  # 5d7d
- op: discuss  # 04ec
  at: '2026-06-25T02:33:56Z'  # 04ec
  by: agent  # 04ec
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 04ec
  clock: 6  # 04ec
  nonce: 04ec  # 04ec
  message: "IMPLEMENTATION SPEC for the F1+F4 co-release (human-approved 2026-06-24: model=one-file-node-universe + non-source view; invariant=centrality keys SUBSET of node paths; rename centrality_scores -> additional_file_centrality_scores; do NOT build whole-graph centrality (already in `hypergumbo symbols` via ranking.compute_centrality); reconcile sketch_precomputed status toward INTERNAL, keep in schema marked internal, clean rename). SCOPE refinement: anchor the ADDITIONAL-FILE CANDIDATE cohort (is_additional_file_candidate = CONFIG/DOCUMENTATION role, taxonomy.py:721) = the centrality keys; source files already anchored (WI-dagif). Binaries/data/unknown excluded (get_language returns None -> no valid make_file_id) -- the clean reading of D15 \"every file\". COMPONENTS: (1) F4 core, cli.py:8242-8245: source_paths must be CONTENT-only (sym.kind != \"file\") else anchoring docs/configs subtracts them from candidate_files (cli.py:8260) and empties Additional-Files. (2) F1 anchoring: KEY ORDERING FINDING -- finalize() at cli.py:8153 serializes behavior_map[\"nodes\"] from ranked_symbols; the sketch_precomputed/centrality block is at 8234 (AFTER finalize). So anchors MUST be minted BEFORE finalize or they never reach nodes (subset would fail). Cleanest site = the all_analyzers chokepoint (analyze/all_analyzers.py:346-376, where synthesize_file_anchors_for_node_bearing_paths already runs, well before ranking+finalize); it can reach the discovered files via discovery.get_file_index().all_files() and repo_root. Mint a kind=file anchor per candidate path lacking one, language via taxonomy.get_language(path) (skip if None), real span.end_line via _read_file_end_line. (3) Extract shared helper additional_file_candidates(repo_root, all_files, content_source_paths) (filter: skip content paths, skip hidden, is_additional_file_candidate, DEFAULT_EXCLUDES+ADDITIONAL_FILES_EXCLUDES patterns) used by BOTH the anchoring site AND cli.py centrality -- single source of truth (mind the import graph: is_additional_file_candidate=taxonomy, DEFAULT_EXCLUDES=discovery, ADDITIONAL_FILES_EXCLUDES=sketch). (4) Rename centrality_scores -> additional_file_centrality_scores: producer cli.py:8299/8304, consumers sketch.py:6460/6462/6610/6614 (the cached_centrality_scores PARAMETER name can stay internal). (5) Subset property test: every additional_file_centrality_scores key is a node path (holds by construction post-F1). (6) Schema reconcile: fix generate-schema:296-303 comment (drop \"documented contract\" claim for sketch_precomputed; state internal/unstable per spec.md:706), rename the field in the generate-schema:441-477 overlay, mark internal; regenerate docs/schema.json + baseline. (7) Test fallout: corpus-wide node addition for config/doc fixtures -> content-node-filter updates (kind!=file) like the WI-dagif round + any centrality_scores->additional_file_centrality_scores test refs. Closes WI-rajod, INV-napap, INV-jifus centrality face, WI-mutuv (supply_chain_summary file-anchor count), WI-rikaz (centrality semantics doc). Scope/value verified across two scoping Workflows (lab notebooks notebookjournal_06242026_0440.md + the file-anchor-f1-scope run)."  # 04ec
