  nonce: c0cb  # c0cb
  message: "Implemented file-anchor:F1+F4 co-release in commit 037a3730de (origin/dev). Behavioral evidence — live repro on packages/hypergumbo-lang-rust-analyzer: 13 file-anchor nodes, additional_file_centrality_scores={README.md}, README.md IS a file node path, subset invariant (keys subset of file node paths) HOLDS, legacy 'centrality_scores' key absent. F1 mints a kind=file anchor for every additional-file candidate (CONFIG/DOC role, resolvable language, real file) at the all_analyzers chokepoint via taxonomy.additional_file_candidates + synthesize_file_anchors_for_paths; F4 makes cli.py's candidate selection content-only (kind!=file) so the anchors are not re-subtracted from the Additional-Files surface. Both sites share the same selector, so every centrality key is a file-anchor node path by construction. Production-path test test_run_behavior_map.py::test_additional_file_candidate_anchored_and_subset_invariant_f1_f4 locks it. Two fallout root causes fixed structurally: path-form-robust minter dedup (html emits ABSOLUTE file paths normalized only downstream) and additional_file_candidates skips broken symlinks (Path.is_file). The node-bearing half was WI-dagif; this closes the nodeless config/doc cohort. All changed source files at 100% coverage."  # c0cb
